  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Three blocks <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> are pulled on a horizontal smooth surface by a force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> as shown in figure. The tensions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> in the string are respectively:</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0036_a1519ff77b5e.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 56px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mn>40</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>64</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo> </mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mn>88</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>96</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>100</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Since, the length of the string will remain same. Hence, all blocks will have the same acceleration.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0036_3fe25fc5ae77.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 72px;\"/></p><p>Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p><p>Now,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0036_dacf198719bd.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 70px;\"/></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}